  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836102",
      "title": "Dynamic & Conditional Styling with Tailwind",
      "sourceHash": "fd7e13ba2091d84ca03fd26dc66d4ac23fc014018a796da857b7f25f7d2f2e1f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 4.26,
          "en": "Now what about dynamic or conditional styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.26,
          "end": 8.34,
          "en": "as we, for example have it here in our Input component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.34,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "There we wanna change some styles and some colors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 15.153,
          "en": "if the invalid prop is being set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "Well that's also straightforward to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 22.69,
          "en": "Here, we can get rid of these styled components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.96,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "and therefore maybe rename our custom component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 30.3,
          "en": "to just Input again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 33.21,
          "en": "And I'll still accept the label invalid prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.21,
          "end": 34.89,
          "en": "and all the other remaining props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 37.02,
          "en": "but now we're going to switch back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.02,
          "end": 39.16,
          "en": "to the regular built in label here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 43.75,
          "en": "and get rid of this prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 47.16,
          "en": "and switch back to the regular input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.16,
          "end": 51.003,
          "en": "and get rid of this dollar sign invalid prop here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.5,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "And now we of course can again apply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 56.973,
          "en": "some Tailwind utility classes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 60.3,
          "en": "And now to make this less cumbersome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.3,
          "end": 63.69,
          "en": "and make sure that you don't have to type them manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.69,
          "end": 66.75,
          "en": "you'll find this Input.jsx file attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.75,
          "end": 68.82,
          "en": "and you can simply copy its content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 71.07300000000001,
          "en": "into your Input.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "That will give you a label with a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "that includes all the Tailwind classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 79.5,
          "en": "that should be added and an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 82.263,
          "en": "with all the classes that are needed added to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.21000000000001,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "With that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "you will see that label and input changed a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 92.31,
          "en": "But that in general, we got a style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "that's similar to what we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 98.553,
          "en": "with this light gray text, this gray background, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 101.85,
          "en": "We don't have that conditional styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.85,
          "end": 103.953,
          "en": "in case it should be invalid though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "But adjusting these styles conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 110.55,
          "en": "is now actually pretty straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 113.913,
          "en": "We can, for example, create a labelClasses variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 120.32,
          "en": "which includes these label classes here as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.4,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "And then we could add a if check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "and check if invalid is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 129.24,
          "en": "in which case we wanna change those label classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.24,
          "end": 131.043,
          "en": "to a different list of classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 136.353,
          "en": "And then down here we just set the labelClasses as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.49,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "Now here in this case, the classes are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 141.093,
          "en": "of course mostly the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 144.903,
          "en": "So therefore I can copy it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "And then I just want to change the text color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "from text-stone to a different color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "And therefore I'll not copy text-stone down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 159.933,
          "en": "but instead set a separate color of text-red-400,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 162.243,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.92000000000002,
          "end": 165.93,
          "en": "And with that you'll see that if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.93,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "if I submit this form in an invalid state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 170.403,
          "en": "the labels become red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.45,
          "end": 174.57,
          "en": "And that's how you can apply styles conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.57,
          "end": 176.52,
          "en": "with Tailwind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.52,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "Now of course, repeating all these styles here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.74,
          "en": "which are exactly the same styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.74,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "no matter if invalid is true or false is a bit cumbersome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 188.49,
          "en": "Therefore, a slightly better alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 192.57,
          "en": "is to set up a base labelClasses string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.57,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "that does not include text-stone-300,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 199.743,
          "en": "but only all the base classes, which don't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.03,
          "end": 204.51,
          "en": "And then to just add this red-text color here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.51,
          "end": 206.67000000000002,
          "en": "if invalid is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.67000000000002,
          "end": 211.67000000000002,
          "en": "And else add this text-stone-300 class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 217.71,
          "en": "with a white space in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.71,
          "end": 221.13,
          "en": "so that there is a white space after the last class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.13,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "that is set up in the base classes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 226.26,
          "en": "So this white space here is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 228.93,
          "en": "so that this does not become one long class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.93,
          "end": 231.09300000000002,
          "en": "but instead two separate classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.95,
          "end": 234.54,
          "en": "But that's now an elegant way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.54,
          "end": 238.35,
          "en": "of setting different classes based on some base classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.35,
          "end": 240.273,
          "en": "depending on a certain condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.83,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "Now we can do the same for our input, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 247.353,
          "en": "We can set up a input classes string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.57,
          "end": 252.03,
          "en": "which in the end is this string here of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.03,
          "end": 254.05,
          "en": "So we can cut this and set it up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.72,
          "end": 258.9,
          "en": "and then we can adjust these input classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.9,
          "end": 263.52,
          "en": "if invalid is true by concatenating more classes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.52,
          "end": 267.303,
          "en": "and doing the same if invalid is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.83,
          "end": 272.01,
          "en": "Now for the input, it's more than just the text color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.01,
          "end": 275.103,
          "en": "that needs to change, but it's also the text color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.27,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "So we can cut this here from our base classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 283.68,
          "en": "and add this here if invalid is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.68,
          "end": 285.363,
          "en": "So as a default style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.74,
          "end": 289.14300000000003,
          "en": "And do the same for the background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 294.423,
          "en": "Cut that here and add it here if invalid is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 298.38,
          "en": "If invalid is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.38,
          "end": 303.38,
          "en": "I instead want to add text-red-500 here, bg-red-100,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 306.99,
          "end": 309.813,
          "en": "and border-red-300.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 312.03,
          "end": 315.57,
          "en": "And with that again, we can use these input classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 315.57,
          "end": 319.2,
          "en": "down here as a value for class name on the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 319.2,
          "end": 322.173,
          "en": "so that our JSX code is pretty lean again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 323.04,
          "end": 325.44,
          "en": "And we got all this styling code up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 325.44,
          "end": 328.41,
          "en": "where we then add certain Tailwind classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 328.41,
          "end": 329.823,
          "en": "depending on a condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 330.99,
          "end": 334.62,
          "en": "And with that, if we save that, we got the default look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 334.62,
          "end": 337.08299999999997,
          "en": "And if I click sign in, we got the invalid look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 338.49,
          "end": 342.06,
          "en": "And with that we migrated almost the entire app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.06,
          "end": 345.42,
          "en": "Now it's just the background of these inputs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 345.42,
          "end": 348.33299999999997,
          "en": "that needs to change and the second button here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}